---
title: Ham, brie and fig grilled cheese
servings: 2
tags: [pork, quick]
source: Ham, Brie, and Fig Preserve Grilled Cheese by Bonne Maman, https://bonnemaman.us/blogs/recipe/ham-brie-and-fig-preserve-grilled-cheese
---

Butter one side of each slice of
@bread{4%slices}(rustic white such as ciabatta, boule or sourdough, cut thick)
with the @butter{2%tbsp}.

Lay two slices buttered side down in a #skillet{} over medium-low heat. Spread
the @dijon mustard{1%tsp} on top, then layer half the
@brie cheese{8%oz}(cold, sliced ¼ inch thick), the @ham{4%slices} and the rest
of the brie.

Spread the @fig preserves{1-1.5%tbsp} on the unbuttered side of the other two
slices and set them on top, buttered side up.

Cook until golden on both sides and the brie has melted. Rest ~{2%minutes},
then cut on the diagonal.
